        <mxCell id="UTYBNJX3NSuSBxuMePmN-23" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=16;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;font-size: 16px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px&quot;&gt;Transactions are part of a block and have&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;incoming transfers and/or an outgoing transfer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;font-size: 16px&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px&quot;&gt;The outgoing transfer may have destination amounts and addresses which are saved locally with the wallet and are not recoverable from the blockchain.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;font-size: 16px&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px&quot;&gt;Transactions may also have outputs received by the wallet when requested.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;font-size: 16px&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px&quot;&gt;In the JSON of monero-c these parents are not fields. A tx comes in the txs of its block, {&quot;blocks&quot;:[...]}, a transfer and an output in the tx that has them, and a tx that the wallet made in the txs of its tx set, {&quot;txSets&quot;:[...]}.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="416" width="775.5" x="38.25" y="14885" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
