        <mxCell id="s671" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=12;fontFamily=Verdana;" value="&lt;b&gt;How to read the C tables&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Every function returns monero_result: MONERO_OK, or MONERO_ERROR with the message in monero_last_error() and the kind in monero_last_error_code().&lt;br&gt;The first parameter of a daemon or wallet function is its handle, monero_daemon* or monero_wallet*, and the rows leave it out. A result comes back in an out_* parameter, and the row gives its type after the colon. A model is JSON text with the field names of the types below, which the caller frees with monero_utils_free(), and a secret is freed with monero_utils_free_secret(). A parameter with =null is a pointer, and NULL means none." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="124" width="814" x="17.5" y="10" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
